Sally,

I think I've read a bit of Rumi; perhaps when Gary was sending out his poetry
stuff. I am not familiar with Carl Krieg and look forward to what you send
my way.

I met a guy yesterday at the race I ran. He won the division I'm in (70+ year
olds). He is a Math / Physics PhD and is interested in cosmology. Your "So
I say let consciousness evolve and expand whenever possible just as the cosmos
does." and a bit later, "The afterlife happens when other people's consciousness
is built on yours." can't be better said. I said something *very* similar
to my neighbor the other day. He started the conversation by saying he was
pretty sure I didn't believe in an afterlife. Your "Not everyone has an 'afterlife'"
is awesome.

Anyway, again, I was quite taken by your long response to the Michener quote.
I am not sure these are actually his words but I can't find any other source.

I have read a lot of Steinbeck. I fairly recently read East of Eden (I really
don't remember much of it but I do remember liking it a lot). I read it shortly
after reading Milton's Paradise Lost and the parallels were strong. I will
have to reread it.

Love,

Lee
