/* calculation and mine differ by about two 1000ths of a second. So, I would say you are "fairly 
/* accurate" with your age estimation today.

/* siad.tc - 2/17/9 - tct - seconds in a day (days in a second)

/* 2147483647 is the largest integer (under 32-bit Linux tiny-c interpreter)

dpf int n,d,p [
  /* display proper fraction n/d as decimal number
  /* with p digit precision 
  int w
  w=10*n/d
  if (p) [
    pnp w
    dpf(10*n%d,d,p-1) /* recursive call
    ]
  ]

pnp int n [ /* pn sans leading space
  MC n,14
  ]

siad [
  hilo '1';color '6';pl "";ps "siad.tc (seconds in a day) - tct - 2/17/9";pl "";color '7'
  int w,u
  u=60*60*24 /* seconds per day
  w=u*365 /* seconds per year
  pl "";ps "1 day equals ";pn u;ps " seconds."
  pl "";ps "1 year equals ";pn w;ps " seconds."
  pl "";ps "1 second equals .";dpf(1,u,31);ps " days."
  pl "";ps "1 second equals .";dpf(1,w,31);ps " years."
  pl ""
  int i1;i1=819178082 /* DeeDee
  int i2;i2=818617450 /* Max
  int s,t
  pl "";ps "DeeDee's (TcT's) estimate of her age is 38.819178082 years." 
  pl "";ps "Max's estimate of DeeDee's age is 38.818617450 years." 
  pl "";ps "The difference between DeeDee's and Max's estimate"
  pl "is (approx.) .000";pnp (i1-i2);ps " years."
  pl ""
  s=(i1-i2)*w/100000 
  t=(i1-i2)*w%100000 
  pl "This equals, approx.,";pn s;ps ".";dpf t,100000,2;ps " seconds."
  pl ""
  ]  
eel like that for the entire race.  But
I began to tank during the second loop.  Sweating bullets and so thirsty.
 Thank God for Sherry, who gave me a Gu and an ice cold A & W root beer at
about mile 14.  I think I would've been crawling the whole third loop without
it.  Stomach a mess after the race.  Not sure if it's dehydration or a bug.
 Ironically, Sofie is sick too - threw up this morning and is lethargic now.
 About to try some coconut water recommended by Vanessa (for both of us).
 I can't believe I out-dripped Lea, though my weight was down 5 lbs. and
that was after consuming a fattening McDonald's vanilla milkshake!

ceb - Monday, September 19, 2016 at 02:33:15 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Referring toi an expression of Tracy's I "bonked" it this week with my running
Took Monday and Tuesday off.  Skipped Wednesday... Crazy buzy
Ran 4.92 Thursday,  Pace 9:44 / mile

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1368340961>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1368340961</a>

Skipped Friday.

Ran with Concord Runners Satuday and shortened my run returning with Richard Fortier
on an earlier return route.  We both didn't have too much in the tank Saturday.

10.72 miles tonight (Sunday) in 1:52:47.  Pace 10:20 / mile
Was going to do 14 but ran out of steam and roads were getting too dark for
running 

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1368498467>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1368498467</a>

weekly mileage ~ 20.67 which includes an approximate 5 miles with Concord
Runners.  Forgot to start my watch at start.  About 11 miles short of plan.

MCT - Monday, September 19, 2016 at 10:45:46 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Did 8 muggy miles this morning. Logy is the only way to describe it. Fall
Festival sounded sounded like Fall Torture! Good thing I missed it because
I would have melted down worse than you guys. 

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1368829396>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1368829396</a>
<img src=RSAS.JPG> <img src=FH.JPG>

