ХН␀б#^␀#е6␀бСБЙ~#ю (ъ+·ЙНН}                         NOTES ON INSTALLATION

Options ---

When you move the cursor to a new line, the disk is automatically updated
with any changes to the current filename unless you elect to receive a
warning message first.  File attributes F5-F7 are reserved by the DOS and
should never be changed.  If you set the lockout, any changes you make to
those attributes are ignored.  "Attribute Labels" are your personal reminders
of attr usage.  "Illegal characters" are those not accepted in CP/M file
names (per Digital Research).  If you shorten the list, repeat the final
character until the patching buffer fills.

Commands ---

Most of the commands can be installed as single control characters or as
meta-key/control combinations.  Fixed commands are listed at the bottom of
the patching screen.

␀Н}Strike Any Key --  Н±ГvНН}
     Letters in the table below represent CONTROL KEYS.  Those followed
 by a "#" are shifted keys which are scanned only after the lead-in key
 has been pressed.  Each command must be assigned a unique key.

 Cursor Movement:  ^E  Up,  ^D  Rt,  ^X  Dn,  ^S  Lt   (Or Arrow Keys)    
 Quit: "."  Skip: <sp>  To Enter CR/ ESC/ DEL/ TAB Use Key   Disable = "-"␀НДН}Fixed Commands:
   "." - Switch filename/type field
  <sp> - Advance in attribute field
 S,R,T - Set, Reset, Toggle an attribute␀ЙНН}
